00:12:44.250 --> 00:12:45.930
that they've got.

00:12:45.930 --> 00:12:50.940
And so this vision of the
intelligent workspace,

00:12:50.940 --> 00:12:53.490
we make the assumption
that the user

00:12:53.490 --> 00:12:57.090
is going to need to be able to
access those resources wherever

00:12:57.090 --> 00:12:58.950
they happen to be.

00:12:58.950 --> 00:13:01.950
So we take the
perimeter that used

00:13:01.950 --> 00:13:05.760
to be the corporate firewall
at your primary data

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:07.130
center for an organization.

00:13:07.130 --> 00:13:09.330
And we're essentially
moving that perimeter.

00:13:09.330 --> 00:13:13.320
Instead of being at the edge
of a business or a data center,

00:13:13.320 --> 00:13:17.740
we're moving that perimeter out
around the actual user itself.

00:13:17.740 --> 00:13:21.300
So the Citrix of today, we
count over 400,000 customers.

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:23.250
And those are customers
as in businesses.

00:13:23.250 --> 00:13:27.810
We don't really have any
consumer-facing technologies

00:13:27.810 --> 00:13:30.080
in the market today.

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:32.580
We've got coverage through a
large percentage of the Fortune

00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:33.820
500.

00:13:33.820 --> 00:13:37.260
And ultimately, we've got over
100 million licensed users

00:13:37.260 --> 00:13:38.920
out in the market space.

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:40.760
So we've grown a heck of a lot.

00:13:40.760 --> 00:13:43.290
And along the way,
as I've mentioned,

00:13:43.290 --> 00:13:47.130
we historically probably
very similar to you

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:49.620
had been building services
and building products

00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:51.870
that we've been shipping
kind of traditionally, right?

00:13:51.870 --> 00:13:54.927
So fall in the old
traditional waterfall model.

00:13:54.927 --> 00:13:56.760
Building package products
that we would then

00:13:56.760 --> 00:14:00.540
test, and put in a box, and
actually ship people a box.

00:14:00.540 --> 00:14:05.160
So over time we've been
on pretty substantial

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:07.320
digital transformation
of our own.

00:14:07.320 --> 00:14:09.390
Moving our own business
away from that model

00:14:09.390 --> 00:14:11.760
of delivering perpetual
products and moving

00:14:11.760 --> 00:14:15.543
into the delivery of those
technologies via services.

00:14:15.543 --> 00:14:17.460
So you'll hear us talk
about this thing called

00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:19.540
Citrix Cloud today.

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:22.240
And I want to ensure you
that this is not an IS.

00:14:22.240 --> 00:14:24.270
You're not going to
go buy some compute,

00:14:24.270 --> 00:14:26.950
and some networking, and
some storage from us.

00:14:26.950 --> 00:14:29.350
So Citrix Cloud is
our platform that we

00:14:29.350 --> 00:14:32.830
leverage to deliver all
these innovative services

00:14:32.830 --> 00:14:34.580
to our customers.

00:14:34.580 --> 00:14:37.550
So this platform is cloud-based.

00:14:37.550 --> 00:14:40.180
We're doing all the
similar types of things

00:14:40.180 --> 00:14:43.570
with rapid iteration, and
release cycles, and canarying

00:14:43.570 --> 00:14:46.270
of releases, and all of
those kinds of things

00:14:46.270 --> 00:14:49.510
that you're probably
also dealing with.

00:14:49.510 --> 00:14:51.610
But with this
cloud-based platform,

00:14:51.610 --> 00:14:53.450
we're pre-integrating
the services.

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:56.890
So you can consume multiple
different services on their own

00:14:56.890 --> 00:14:58.630
to solve point problems.

00:14:58.630 --> 00:15:02.110
Or you can consume
multiple services together

00:15:02.110 --> 00:15:05.470
and the platform itself
integrates those services

00:15:05.470 --> 00:15:07.743
and saves you from
a lot of the work.

00:15:07.743 --> 00:15:09.160
Then we're also
with the platform,

00:15:09.160 --> 00:15:11.110
managing, and maintaining,
and upgrading,

00:15:11.110 --> 00:15:13.690
and keeping evergreen
all the components that

00:15:13.690 --> 00:15:16.660
go into this solution.

00:15:16.660 --> 00:15:18.610
But one point I'll make
here is that Citrix

00:15:18.610 --> 00:15:22.153
has a lot of experience from
our digital transformation.

00:15:22.153 --> 00:15:24.070
One kind of unique thing
that we've been doing

00:15:24.070 --> 00:15:27.190
is taking those experiences
and our lessons learned

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:30.700
and rolling those into features
and capabilities of our cloud

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:32.120
