00:45:10.320 --> 00:45:12.100
So they deployed four instance.

00:45:12.100 --> 00:45:13.240
The Cloud Connector.

00:45:13.240 --> 00:45:15.740
The CC is the Cloud Connector
we've been talking about.

00:45:15.740 --> 00:45:18.260
The DC is a Domain Controller,
an Active Directory Domain

00:45:18.260 --> 00:45:19.107
Controller.

00:45:19.107 --> 00:45:20.690
The third one, which
is shut down now,

00:45:20.690 --> 00:45:21.520
we called it management.

00:45:21.520 --> 00:45:23.000
It really was just
a script runner.

00:45:23.000 --> 00:45:26.720
It ran the scripts that actually
configured Citrix Cloud.

00:45:26.720 --> 00:45:29.910
So once it was done, there
was nothing else to do,

00:45:29.910 --> 00:45:30.920
so it shuts itself down.

00:45:30.920 --> 00:45:32.930
The way we've set
up this deployment.

00:45:32.930 --> 00:45:38.610
And then the XA, that's
the VDA server right there.

00:45:38.610 --> 00:45:40.970
And so this is that
simple architecture

00:45:40.970 --> 00:45:44.180
we looked at, where we've got
a Cloud Connector, the Domain

00:45:44.180 --> 00:45:49.040
Controller, and a
small VDA fleet.

00:45:49.040 --> 00:45:51.907
Now if you want to log into
this environment that's

00:45:51.907 --> 00:45:53.990
been set up for you, one
thing that you have to do

00:45:53.990 --> 00:45:56.450
is acquire some
user credentials.

00:45:56.450 --> 00:45:58.250
We have pre-populated
the Active Directory

00:45:58.250 --> 00:46:00.860
domain with some sample users.

00:46:00.860 --> 00:46:06.080
And so there is a PowerShell
script in that same directory

00:46:06.080 --> 00:46:15.570
that we were in before
called get domain users.

00:46:21.140 --> 00:46:23.600
And what it will do
is it will reach out

00:46:23.600 --> 00:46:26.710
to Google Cloud Storage.

00:46:26.710 --> 00:46:29.140
Now first it's going to ask
us which deployment do we want

00:46:29.140 --> 00:46:30.307
to retrieve these users for.

00:46:30.307 --> 00:46:32.770
Because you can actually
have multiple of these sample

00:46:32.770 --> 00:46:35.110
deployments running
in your project.

00:46:35.110 --> 00:46:38.170
The one we just ran
is number five here.

00:46:38.170 --> 00:46:41.380
It's going to reach out
to Google Cloud Storage

00:46:41.380 --> 00:46:43.360
and retrieve an
encrypted blob where

00:46:43.360 --> 00:46:46.870
we have stored the usernames and
passwords of some sample users.

00:46:46.870 --> 00:46:49.370
And then it's going to decrypt
that blob using our KMS

00:46:49.370 --> 00:46:49.870
service.

00:46:49.870 --> 00:46:52.000
So we've stored that
not in plain text,

00:46:52.000 --> 00:46:54.130
but as an encrypted blob.

00:46:54.130 --> 00:46:57.867
And here we can see the
usernames and passwords.

00:46:57.867 --> 00:46:59.950
So let's just say we're
going to log in as user 5.

00:46:59.950 --> 00:47:01.930
I'm copying that
password for user 5.

00:47:01.930 --> 00:47:05.260
And we can bring up
the Citrix Workspace.

00:47:05.260 --> 00:47:08.770
And fingers crossed, we should
be able to say we want to log

00:47:08.770 --> 00:47:14.830
in as user_5@example.org
and paste that password in.

00:47:14.830 --> 00:47:16.360
And that Citrix Workspace.

00:47:16.360 --> 00:47:18.695
Now remember, this is
going to Citrix Cloud,

00:47:18.695 --> 00:47:21.070
through the Cloud Connector,
against our Active Directory

00:47:21.070 --> 00:47:22.310
Domain Controller.

00:47:22.310 --> 00:47:25.060
We have successfully
logged in now.

00:47:25.060 --> 00:47:26.980
If we go look at
View All Apps, we

00:47:26.980 --> 00:47:28.390
should see Notepad was set up.

00:47:28.390 --> 00:47:31.960
We are authorized to use
the Virtual App Notepad.

00:47:31.960 --> 00:47:34.510
And if we click on
that, that, again,

00:47:34.510 --> 00:47:39.030
should send that request
to initialize the session

00:47:39.030 --> 00:47:41.530
through Citrix Cloud, through
the session brokering,

00:47:41.530 --> 00:47:44.380
through Cloud Connector to
launch the session on the VDA.

00:47:44.380 --> 00:47:46.780
Here we see it's logging in.

00:47:46.780 --> 00:47:50.920
And momentarily what we
should see on a Chromebook now

00:47:50.920 --> 00:47:54.730
is a window that pops up to
let us access our Windows

00:47:54.730 --> 00:47:58.960
app, which is Notepad.

00:47:58.960 --> 00:48:02.020
And this environment, was
